Test Case 1:

Find the primary constants R,L,G and C for the varying values of Characteristic Impedance (Zo) of a Transmission Line at a frequency f=2 Khz. Vary the Characteristic Impedance valup from 1()() O and take five readings at the interval of 2() O. Keep the Propagation Constant (7) constant.

AIM: To find the primary constants R,L,G and C for the varying values of Characteristic Impedance (Zo) of a Transmission Line at a frequency f=2 Khz. Vary the Characteristic Impedance valuel from 100 Q and take five readings at the interval of 2() Q. Keep the Propagation Constant (y) constant

CODE:
clear;
clc;
Zo = 100.6;
f = 2000;
// Propagation constant
P = 0.054exp(%i(87.9*%pi/180));
w = 2*%pif;
// Calculate Z = R + jωL
Z = ZoP;
R = real(Z);
L = imag(Z)/w;
printf('Resistance R = %f ohms/km\n', R);
printf('Inductance L = %f mH/km\n', L10^3);
// Calculate Y = G + jωC
Y = P/Zo;
G = real(Y);
C = imag(Y)/w;
printf('Conductance G = %f micromhos/km\n', G10^6);
printf('Capacitance C = %f microfarads/km\n', C*10^6);

